# What must NOT go into the packaged .apworld.
#
# Archipelago's own "Build APWorlds" launcher component reads this, and the
# spec calls that component "the correct way to package your .apworld". Until
# this file existed, only tools/build_apworld.py knew to leave these out - so
# the two packagers produced DIFFERENT archives from the same source, and the
# sanctioned one shipped a test suite and a yaml that do not belong in a
# player's install.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE ONE LIST. tools/build_apworld.py reads it rather than
# keeping its own copy, which is the whole point - the two packagers
# disagreeing is the bug this file was added to fix, and a second list to
# 'keep in step' would reintroduce it.
#
# The global list already covers __pycache__, .DS_Store, __MACOSX, .git,
# .gitignore, archipelago.json and .apignore itself, so this only adds ours.

# The world's own tests import Archipelago's test harness, which a player's
# install does not have on the import path.
test/

# The shipped player template is a RELEASE asset handed to the player
# separately, not something the world imports. It lives in the package so a
# test can hold it in step with ALTTLOptions.
player.yaml
